== Where to view and edit shortcuts ==

On FreeCAD {{Version|1.1}} (including 1.1.1):

# Select {{MenuCommand|Tools &rarr; [[Std_DlgCustomize|Customize...]]}}.
# Open the {{MenuCommand|Keyboard}} tab.
# Pick a {{MenuCommand|Category}} (File, Edit, View, Sketcher, ...).
# The list shows '''Icon''', '''Command''', '''Shortcut''' (current), and '''Default'''.
# Select a command, click {{MenuCommand|New shortcut}}, press the key or sequence, then {{Button|Assign}}.

Later FreeCAD builds that use calendar version numbers may move this UI under Preferences ([[Preferences_Editor#Keyboard|Preferences Editor]]). That is not FreeCAD 1.1.1.

=== Tips ===

* Search by command name or by shortcut text. Multi-key sequences: comma and space ({{Value|g, l}}). Single letters: parentheses ({{Value|(c)}}).
* {{MenuCommand|Multi-key sequence delay}} is the wait between keys in a sequence (often {{Value|300}} ms).
* {{Button|Reset}} restores one command; {{Button|Reset All}} restores all defaults.
* If a shortcut does nothing, switch to the workbench that owns the command or show its toolbar.
* Some bindings are easy to miss, such as workbench switching ({{KEY|W}} then {{KEY|1}}...{{KEY|9}} after you order workbenches) and draw-style sequences.

== How multi-key shortcuts work ==

FreeCAD shortcuts use Qt. Two common forms:

* '''Modifier chord:''' hold modifiers and press a key, for example {{KEY|Ctrl}}+{{KEY|S}} (Save). Same idea as most desktop apps and SolidWorks file/edit chords.
* '''Key sequence''' (multi-key): press and '''release''' one key, then press the next before the multi-key delay ends, for example {{KEY|V}} then {{KEY|F}} (Fit all). The UI usually shows this as {{Value|V, F}}.

A sequence is not a chord. Do not hold {{KEY|V}} and {{KEY|F}} together: press {{KEY|V}}, release, then {{KEY|F}}.

=== Limits ===

* At most '''four''' key presses in one sequence.
* If you start a sequence and abandon it, the next keys may be ignored until the sequence times out or fails. Press the first key again, or wait for the timeout.
* Letter-only sequences are mostly workbench tools, so they stay out of the way of global {{KEY|Ctrl}} chords.

=== Prefix design (how to remember them) ===

Default sequences often use a first key as a group label. That is only a naming habit in the defaults, not a separate mode:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Prefix !! Typical meaning !! Examples
|-
| {{KEY|V}} || View || {{KEY|V}} {{KEY|F}} fit all; {{KEY|V}} {{KEY|S}} fit selection; {{KEY|V}} {{KEY|1}}...{{KEY|7}} draw styles
|-
| {{KEY|G}} || Sketcher geometry || {{KEY|G}} {{KEY|L}} line; {{KEY|G}} {{KEY|C}} circle; {{KEY|G}} {{KEY|R}} rectangle
|-
| {{KEY|K}} || Sketcher constraints (less common ones) || {{KEY|K}} {{KEY|D}} distance; {{KEY|K}} {{KEY|A}} angle
|-
| {{KEY|Z}} || Sketcher tools / helpers || {{KEY|Z}} {{KEY|T}} offset; {{KEY|Z}} {{KEY|M}} move
|-
| {{KEY|T}} || Tree view options (global) || {{KEY|T}} {{KEY|1}}... sync options; {{KEY|T}} {{KEY|G}} go to selection
|-
| {{KEY|P}} || CAM / Path tools || {{KEY|P}} {{KEY|J}} job; {{KEY|P}} {{KEY|P}} post process
|-
| Single letters || Frequent sketcher constraints || {{KEY|T}} tangent; {{KEY|H}} horizontal; {{KEY|E}} equal
|}

Second keys are often mnemonic ({{KEY|L}} line, {{KEY|C}} circle), but not always. Some letters are leftovers after better ones were already taken.

From SolidWorks: sketch tools are often one key while a sketch is active. FreeCAD Sketcher more often uses {{KEY|G}}... for geometry and keeps many constraints as single keys.

